{"id": "5d3040c20c143e436cc113d8", "name": "Okrum: Ke3chang group targets diplomatic missions", "description": "The Ke3chang group, also known as APT15, is a threat group believed to be operating out of China. Its activities were traced back to 2010 in FireEye\u2019s 2013 report on operation Ke3chang \u2013 a cyberespionage campaign directed at diplomatic organizations in Europe.\n\nWe have been tracking the malicious activities related to this threat actor and discovered a previously undocumented malware family with strong links to the Ke3chang group \u2013 a backdoor we named Okrum. According to ESET telemetry, Okrum was first detected in December 2016, and targeted diplomatic missions in Slovakia, Belgium, Chile, Guatemala and Brazil throughout 2017.", "author_name": "AlienVault", "modified": "2019-07-18T09:49:54.700000", "created": "2019-07-18T09:49:54.700000", "tags": ["Ke3chang", "china"], "references": ["https://www.welivesecurity.com/2019/07/18/okrum-ke3chang-targets-diplomatic-missions/"], "public": 1, "adversary": "Ke3Chang", "targeted_countries": ["Slovakia", "Belgium", "Chile", "Guatemala", "Brazil"], "malware_families": [], "attack_ids": [], "industries": ["Government"], "TLP": "white", "indicators": [{"id": 1574180420, "indicator": "7c17ccdd8eba3791773de8bc05ab4854421bc3f2554c7ded00065c10698300fe", "type": "FileHash-SHA256", "created": "2019-07-18T09:49:56", "content": "", "title": "", "description": "", "expiration": null, "is_active": 1}, {"id": 393796, "indicator": "6bcf242371315a895298dbe1cdec73805b463c13f9ce8556138fa4fa0a3ad242", "type": "FileHash-SHA256", "created": "2019-07-18T09:49:56", "content": "", "title": "", "description": "", "expiration": null, "is_active": 1}, {"id": 2119469761, "indicator": "02ea0bc17875ab403c05b50205389065283c59e01de55e68cee4cf340ecea046", "type": "FileHash-SHA256", "created": "2019-07-18T09:49:56", "content": "", "title": "", "description": "", "expiration": null, "is_active": 1}, {"id": 2119469762, "indicator": "7b